      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137790,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 357,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cysts are most common in the peripheral iris but also can be free-floating in the anterior chamber or vitreous cavities {19702716}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:00:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137791,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 357,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pigmented epithelial cysts are single or multiple dark-brown lesions that bulge the iris stroma anteriorly and can be detected after mydriasis or via ultrasound biomicroscopy or anterior segment optical coherence tomography at the posterior iris. Drug-associated cysts are smaller and located at the pupillary margin {7070779}.</p>\r\n<p>The clinical differential diagnosis includes: uveitis-associated cysts that arise from interepithelial fluid accumulation in the iris and ciliary body {8976700}, cystic benign naevi, cystic uveal melanoma {6888862}, metastases {28882598}, intraocular foreign body {19702716}, and intraocular parasites {28882598}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:00:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137792,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 357,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These cysts tend to occur in young adults, with one&nbsp;third of cases diagnosed in the third or fourth decade of life {28161919}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:00:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137793,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 357,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pigmented epithelial cysts are idiopathic, but some cases are secondary to longstanding use of miotic or PGF2&alpha;-analogue eye drops {28882598;7070779}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:00:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137794,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 357,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The pathogenesis of medication-related iris cysts is unclear. In contrast to the other cysts, they resolve after discontinuation of the drug {28882598}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:00:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137795,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 357,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dark-brown cysts</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:00:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137796,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 357,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pigmented cysts are lined by a monolayer of iris pigmented epithelial cells, which can be columnar or cuboidal.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:00:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
